%S A399143 5,7,11,6073,6079,6101,6121,6131,6173,6301,6311,6329,6353,6359,6373,
%T A399143 6379,6397,77713,77719,77723,77731,77743,77747,77773,77783,78121,
%U A399143 78193,78203,78697,78707,78721,79229,79231,79273,79279,79283,79309,79319,79397,79399,79411
%N A399143 Primes p for which pi_{24;13,17}(p) - pi_{24;1,5}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A399143 From _Leandro Hector Gallego_ and _Jianing Song_: (Start)
%C A399143 This sequence is about one of the 21 prime races modulo 24 between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see A401958 for more details. Specifically, here we have H = {1,5} and S = {13,17}, corresponding to T = {chi_24, chi_{-24}}, where chi_d = (d/.) is the Kronecker symbol viewed as a character modulo N = 24.
%C A399143 This sequence gives primes p such that Sum_{primes q<=p} (chi_24(q) + chi_{-24}(q))/2 = 1.
%C A399143 Assuming GRH and LI (see A401958), the set of x with pi_{24;13,17}(x) > pi_{24;1,5}(x) has logarithmic density 0.95792, making the race between {1,5} and {13,17} the least biased among the 21 races of cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see the Zenodo preprint below.
%C A399143 Let D(x) = pi_{24;13,17}(x) - pi_{24;1,5}(x). Below x0 = 7*10^12 there are respectively 30659637567, 30659688364, 30659698140, 30659716342, 30659718072, 30659718286, 30659752652, and 30659759379 primes congruent to 1, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, or 23 modulo 24, giving D(x0) = 110427. There are 18 sign-changing zones giving a total of 435086 terms below x0:
%C A399143   (1) a(1..3) = 5-11;
%C A399143   (2) a(4..17) = 6073-6397 (there are 36 primes a(4) <= p <= a(17) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -4 at p = 6221);
%C A399143   (3) a(18..200) = 77713-99347 (there are 985 primes a(18) <= p <= a(200) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -14 at p = 94561);
%C A399143   (4) a(201..327) = 3147101-3171251 (there are 588 primes a(201) <= p <= a(327) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -11 at p = 3167837);
%C A399143   (5) a(328..506) = 4018901-4113143 (there are 1622 primes a(328) <= p <= a(506) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -15 at p = 4104697);
%C A399143   (6) a(507..805) = 50766697-50931841 (there are 3669 primes a(507) <= p <= a(805) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -24 at p = 50857493);
%C A399143   (7) a(806..938) = 61576393-61605697 (there are 929 primes a(806) <= p <= a(938) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -12 at p = 61579873);
%C A399143   (8) a(939..3757) = 66089981-69337559 (there are 84329 primes a(939) <= p <= a(3757) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -82 at p = 68874097);
%C A399143   (9) a(3758..5488) = 83246069-89785937 (there are 87369 primes a(3758) <= p <= a(5488) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -93 at p = 83325821);
%C A399143   (10) a(5489..14029) = 1107955033-1361255333 (there are 7998440 primes a(5489) <= p <= a(14029) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -1069 at p = 1137533281);
%C A399143   (11) a(14030..52141) = 40997318953-43929981353 (there are 55015885 primes a(14030) <= p <= a(52141) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -3151 at p = 41721637829);
%C A399143   (12) a(52142..137165) = 47968650533-51828605527 (there are 44778759 primes a(52142) <= p <= a(137165) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -1595 at p = 49564526309);
%C A399143   (13) a(137166..171990) = 61792500821-67876441573 (there are 106969961 primes a(137166) <= p <= a(171990) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -3537 at p = 62130067177);
%C A399143   (14) a(171991..193463) = 72956879761-73410995717 (there are 9318958 primes a(171991) <= p <= a(193463) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -884 at p = 73381208741);
%C A399143   (15) a(193464..225625) = 81439830673-82635149257 (there are 13906759 primes a(193464) <= p <= a(225625) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -1145 at p = 81923982533);
%C A399143   (16) a(225626..275467) = 739562150641-752272503347 (there are 43898949 primes a(225626) <= p <= a(275467) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -1676 at p = 751294772017);
%C A399143   (17) a(275468..421421) = 850151030473-911782626101 (there are 145989777 primes a(275468) <= p <= a(421421) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -3324 at p = 853785404981);
%C A399143   (18) a(421422..435086) = 972034610453-1102688003771 (there are 4715272455 primes a(421422) <= p <= a(435086) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -19609 at p = 986598078577).
%C A399143 The total number of primes p <= x0 with D(p) < 0 is 5143329473. (End)
